invariant: INV-26
file: quic_aes_soft.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: quic_aes_soft.c stops refusing -DCH_SUITE_AES_GCM, so a tree that
  compiles these sources with its own build system can pair the AES=soft
  S-box with a suite build and hand it a TLS traffic key, AES-128 or
  AES-256. The S-box is indexed with the key, which is the leak INV-26
  exists to keep from a secret. ct.h refuses the same pair, but only in a
  file that reads ct.h, and this one does not; test/quic-builds.sh
  compiles this file alone under the suite define and requires the
  compiler to refuse it.

--- old
#ifdef CH_SUITE_AES_GCM
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM never compiles AES=soft: its S-box is indexed with the key (INV-26)"
#endif
--- new
